course: dictionary
lesson: 15624
title: Tedious: when time drags
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Tedious describes something long, slow and boring, so much that it tires you out. Look at the clues around the word. «The tedious journey took six hours, with traffic jams at every junction.» The journey went on and on, and the jams show why it felt endless.
explain: Tedious can also describe a person. «Mr Hale's tedious lecture made half the class yawn.» Here the lecture is not only long. It makes people bored and a little annoyed. Test your guess by swapping in another word: «a boring lecture» still fits, so tedious is close in meaning to boring.
explain: Tedious is an adjective, so it describes a noun. Its adverb is «tediously» and its noun is «tedium», the feeling of being bored by something that goes on too long. «The tedium of the long queue made Sam sigh.»
fact: Tedious means long, slow and boring.
fact: «Tedious» can also describe a person who is annoying because they are boring.
fact: Tedious is an adjective: tedious, more tedious, most tedious.
fact: «Tediously» is the adverb, and «tedium» is the noun for the feeling of being bored.
fact: In maths, some jobs are tedious, like adding the same number many times, so multiplication can save effort.
exercise: «The tedious journey took six hours, with traffic jams at every junction.» What does tedious mean? | Fast and exciting | Cold and wet | *Long, slow and boring | Short and bumpy
exercise: Priya says adding 5 together ten times is tedious. What could save her effort? | Writing the answer in red | Skipping the sum | Closing her eyes | *Multiplying 5 by 10
exercise: «Mr Hale's tedious lecture made half the class yawn.» Which word is closest in meaning to tedious here? | Thrilling | *Boring | Brief | Colourful
test: Which word is the noun for the feeling of being bored by something that goes on too long? | tedious | tedious-ness | *tedium | tediously
test: «Sam sighed at the tedium of the long queue.» What does tedium mean here? | *The feeling of being bored by something that goes on too long | A large crowd | A happy surprise
exam: Which word means long, slow and boring? | bright | *tedious | tiny | sudden
